    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (2/2 passing, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature on the owner-create flow, placing each piece of logic in its natural home:\n\n1. **API contract** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 Added `registrationDate` as an optional `string`/`format: date` property on the `OwnerFields` schema (mirroring the existing `birthDate` field). Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field is both settable on create and returned on read. The OpenAPI generator maps `format: date` \u2192 `LocalDate`, and Jackson serializes that as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 matching the spec's return format.\n\n2. **Domain model** (`Owner.java`) \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with standard getter/setter and a `toString` entry, consistent with the other properties.\n\n3. **Default logic** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 Added the one create-time rule: when no registration date is supplied, set it to the server's current date (`LocalDate.now()`). This sits alongside the existing create-preparation steps (telephone/email normalization, duplicate check) rather than leaking into unrelated units. The MapStruct mapper needs no change \u2014 it maps `registrationDate` by name automatically in both directions.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); the test profile (`hsqldb`, `ddl-auto=none`) relies on `schema.sql`, so this was required for tests to pass.\n\nBoth acceptance checkpoints pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today when omitted) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (preserves a supplied `2020-06-15`).",
